Yeesh!  I've just read at least six posts (out of 24) asking where people
can get a copy of the spoilers from (or "I can't use the .Z files," or 
"Site xxxx is missing the last section," or many others).  Well...

HERE IS HOW TO GET THE SPOILERS!  (Quite easily, too!)

1) Do _not_ try to get hold of revision level 5.35 of the Spoilers
   (currently the most recent revision level available).
2) Do _not_ send e-mail to the nhspoil@wheaton.UUCP account.

3) Make sure you have at least 300k of free disk space available to
   you.  (This warning especially for those people who have disk quotas
   limiting their disk usage.)
4) Then... wait until November 9th.  After Nov. 9th, make sure you avidly
   read rec.games.hack, because...

ON NOVEMBER 9th, the Wheaton College Nethack Spoiler Team (yeah, that's
basically me), will be releasing a NEW revision (7.xx) of the Spoiler file.
This new revision will be released in at least five parts, and will total
at least 280k (current estimates put the actual release date size at 
closer to 300k).

This new revision will be posted here at Wheaton on the 9th of November,
so should get to you sometime after that.  To give you an idea of how
much time it might take to get to you, this message is being posted on
the 23rd of October.  Figure out how many days this message took to get
to you, and the Spoilers should take roughly the same amount of time.

For those of you who miss parts or all of the new revision on the first
posting, after two weeks, it will be posted a second time.  It will also
be sent to comp.sources.games for posting, where it will be archived by
many sites around the world.

